{
  "$comment": [
    "Copy this to .company.json in the engagement's working directory and fill it in.",
    "",
    "This file binds a session to exactly one company. It lives in the working directory tree and",
    "never in a home directory: a home-level default is the ambient-authority pattern that makes an",
    "operator act on the wrong target, and it is the failure this file prevents.",
    "",
    "Two ways to keep that rule where the working directory IS the home, as in a cloud container:",
    "point XENTHAI_COMPANY at this file, which beats the directory walk and needs no manifest at the",
    "home at all; or, when there is genuinely no other directory, set binding to \"ephemeral\" and",
    "accept what it means — the disk does not survive the session, so the journal has to be uploaded",
    "to the store before it ends, and doctor fails until it is. Leave binding out on a real machine.",
    "",
    "kind says WHOSE store this is: \"client\" (the default, and what an engagement uses) or",
    "\"personal\" for the operator's own material. It changes no veto — a store write is permitted",
    "when a session is bound and refused when it is not, either way. It changes the words the guard",
    "and doctor use, and it stamps every journal row, so a client's audit trail can never be read as",
    "containing the operator's own work or the reverse. An unrecognised value is refused, not",
    "defaulted. For a personal store, approval and regulator carry no meaning; leave them as they are.",
    "",
    "store.kind says WHICH provider holds the store: \"drive\" (Google Drive, the default when absent)",
    "or \"onedrive\" (OneDrive or SharePoint through the Microsoft 365 connector). Declared, never",
    "inferred; an unrecognised value is refused. For a provider whose connector schema the plugin",
    "cannot know in advance, company-new reads the connector's tool schemas in the session and writes",
    "store.tools — the create tool's name and its parameter names for folder, file name and content —",
    "so the upload steps and the transport hook use the connector's real vocabulary. Drive needs none.",
    "",
    "store.root is an ID, never a name. There is no allowlist to maintain: the guard blocks only a",
    "store write with no company bound and a local write outside this directory. Everything else",
    "sensitive is journaled and announced, not blocked. On OneDrive the root may be a Graph path",
    "such as /drive/root:/Clientes/Acme, which is stable and checkable by prefix; a link never is.",
    "",
    "Never commit a filled .company.json to a public repository."
  ],
